 # Workspace Reservation Contract
 
-## Reservation requests
-
-- A reservation request must reject a blank `roomId` after trimming surrounding whitespace.
-- A `memberId` that contains only whitespace is invalid after normalization.
-- `partySize` must be a positive integer.
-- A party larger than the selected room capacity must be rejected.
-- Only active rooms may accept reservations.
-- The request note must be preserved without normalization.
+## Conventions
+
+- All timestamps, including values returned by `now()`, are milliseconds since the Unix epoch.
+- Every time-dependent decision must use the injected `now()` function instead of the system clock.
+
+## Request fields
+
+- A blank `roomId` must be rejected after trimming surrounding whitespace.
+- A `memberId` that contains only whitespace is invalid.
+- `partySize` must be supplied as a number, and that number must be a positive integer.
+- A request window must have an `endAt` value later than its `startAt` value.
+- A request whose `startAt` is earlier than `now()` must be rejected.
+- The request note must be stored exactly as supplied.
+
+## Idempotency
+
+- Idempotency keys are trimmed and lowercased before lookup and storage.
+- The idempotency lookup happens after the request field rules and before any room is selected.
+- If the idempotency key already belongs to a reservation, creation returns that reservation without allocating an identifier or saving another record.
 - New reservation identifiers must come from the injected `nextId` function.
-- Idempotency keys must be trimmed and converted to lowercase before lookup and storage.
-- If the normalized idempotency key already exists, creation must return that reservation without allocating an identifier or saving another record.
-
-## Room selection and availability
-
-- A room must contain every requested amenity; matching only some requested amenities is insufficient.
